<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">empathic-bond</ansi> spell

The <ansi fg="command">Empathic Bond</ansi> spell reaches across the mental divide through
Chrysalis energy, forming a psionic link that calms a creature and
brings it under the caster's influence. Successfully bonded creatures
become loyal companions rather than enemies.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">cast empathic-bond [target]</ansi>

<ansi fg="yellow">Details: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">Type:        </ansi> Harm Single (tame effect)
  <ansi fg="yellow">School:      </ansi> Mental
  <ansi fg="yellow">Base Folds:  </ansi> 16
  <ansi fg="yellow">Conv. Cost:  </ansi> 0
  <ansi fg="yellow">Defense:     </ansi> Mental — the target's willpower resists the bond
  <ansi fg="yellow">Effect:      </ansi> Tames the target creature as a companion

<ansi fg="white-bold">Notes:</ansi>
  - Not all creatures can be tamed — size and nature matter.
  - Strongly-willed creatures are far harder to bond with.

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help spells</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help cast</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help tame</ansi>
